{"availability":"available","full":"StrategicProjects/ruscker","name":"ruscker","description":"Lightweight Rust alternative to ShinyProxy and Shiny Server Free","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":8,"forks":2,"created":"2026-05-23T16:27:08Z","updated":"2026-09-18T23:58:39Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://strategicprojects.github.io/ruscker/","topics":[],"demo":"https://strategicprojects.github.io/ruscker/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:41.879Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:41.879Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:41.879Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T05:50:41.879Z","stars":8,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ruscker is a lightweight, single-binary alternative to ShinyProxy and Shiny Server Free — a portal and orchestrator for containerized web workloads. It serves and load-balances container-per-session interactive apps (R/Shiny, Streamlit, Dash, Voilà, Jupyter, RStudio) and container-per-API stateless HTTP services (Plumber2, FastAPI) behind a single proxy, with a custom landing page and an admin panel. It accepts an existing ShinyProxy application.yml without schema rewrites, while ruscker.yml is the canonical service config, so migration is friction-free.","It ships as a single, ultra-lightweight static binary with instant startup — the idle footprint is about 14 MB.","📖 Documentation: (install · migrate · configure · admin · deploy)."],"features":["Zero-friction migration — bring your apps over with a familiar","Single compiled binary — one artifact to ship and run, with a tiny","Batteries included — a real admin panel, a monitoring dashboard","Anything in a container — interactive apps and stateless HTTP APIs"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/StrategicProjects/ruscker/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5acac235552f62d7ae529498dee5743b50f57dcbd974c4721867adc4a446f94b","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T05:50:42.062Z"},"overviewChec